This product includes ideas, rules and data derived from the following projects.
No source code from them is included; the algorithms were reimplemented in Rust.

- trafilatura (https://github.com/adbar/trafilatura), Apache License 2.0,
  Copyright (C) Adrien Barbaresi and contributors.
  Content-container class/id patterns, boilerplate patterns, the tag whitelist,
  link-density tests and the extraction arbitration heuristics used by the
  article mode (crates/pagesift-content/src/features.rs, article.rs, lib.rs).

- Mozilla Readability (https://github.com/mozilla/readability), Apache License 2.0,
  Copyright (c) 2010 Arc90 Inc and the Mozilla contributors.
  The paragraph scoring, candidate selection and sibling rules
  (crates/pagesift-content/src/readability.rs) and its class/id word lists.

- htmldate (https://github.com/adbar/htmldate), Apache License 2.0,
  Copyright (C) Adrien Barbaresi and contributors.
  The search order, meta attribute lists, date patterns, candidate selection and
  plausibility rules of the publication-date search
  (crates/pagesift-content/src/dates.rs). Its annotated evaluation set is used,
  unmodified and not redistributed, by bench/meta/dates.py.

- courlan (https://github.com/adbar/courlan), Apache License 2.0,
  Copyright (C) Adrien Barbaresi and contributors.
  The tracking-parameter rules used when cleaning crawl URLs
  (crates/pagesift/src/frontier.rs).

- Heritrix (https://github.com/internetarchive/heritrix3), Apache License 2.0,
  Copyright (C) Internet Archive.
  The session-ID stripping and pathological-path rules of the crawl frontier
  (crates/pagesift/src/frontier.rs).

- Scrapy (https://github.com/scrapy/scrapy), BSD 3-Clause License,
  Copyright (c) Scrapy developers.
  The retry policy (status codes, retry count, rescheduling instead of waiting)
  of the crawler (crates/pagesift/src/crawl.rs).

The URL rewrite-rule learning follows the DUST idea from Bar-Yossef, Keidar and
Schonfeld, "Do not crawl in the DUST: different URLs with similar text" (WWW 2007),
and Dasgupta et al., "De-duping URLs via rewrite rules" (KDD 2008).

- markup5ever (https://github.com/servo/html5ever), MIT OR Apache-2.0.
  The HTML named character reference table (crates/pagesift-html/src/entities.rs).
